    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** lineup is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (77.82), both of whom present as elite daily plays. **Gunnar Henderson** holds the highest score today, benefiting from a soft matchup against Ober (4.78 xERA) and his high-upside ability to exploit a slow SP delivery, which is critical for our focus on stolen bases. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** capitalizes on a strong order slot and a favorable platoon matchup against the lefty Patrick Sandoval. Similarly, **Luis Robert Jr.** (76.18) is a core piece of today's strategy; his dynamic platoon edge against the southpaw P\u00e9rez creates a significant lift to his base projection, making him a cornerstone for our production in the middle of the order.\n\nTactical depth is provided by **Jacob Wilson** (72.73) and **Kyle Tucker** (71.02), both of whom are projected for strong outputs. **Jacob Wilson** draws a favorable park and an exploitable matchup against Martinez. The most difficult personnel decision was benching **Jackson Merrill** (38.94), who fell below our 40.0 efficiency threshold due to a difficult draw against a tough arm in Kyle Harrison. Meanwhile, **Nasim Nunez** (48.11) was the closest to cracking the starting nine but was ultimately relegated to the bench in favor of higher-floor options like **Sam Antonacci**, as the optimizer prioritized overall offensive efficiency over Nunez\u2019s specialized speed profile in this specific matchup context.\n\nWe are monitoring weather volatility carefully as we head into the afternoon. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (61.73) and **Heliot Ramos** (52.06) are currently cleared for the lineup despite a 31% rain risk in their respective contest. Their scores remain high enough to justify the risk, though they bear watching if the forecast worsens before first pitch. While **Andy Pages** (66.84) and **Miguel Vargas** (63.34) occupy strong roles, their utility depends on maintaining their projected lineup positions. We remain confident in this configuration as we hunt for volume across our five categories, particularly with **Drake Baldwin** and **Liam Hicks** providing necessary stability at the catcher spots to round out the bottom of our order.",
